        title: 'Confirmation Bias',
        body: 'The tendency to search for, interpret, and remember information that confirms existing beliefs. In corporate strategy, it manifests as management commissioning market research after the decision has been made — to confirm, not test. Kodak\'s engineers invented the digital camera in 1975 but management actively avoided investigating whether digital would replace film because the answer was unwelcome. The debiasing technique: appoint a "red team" explicitly tasked with proving the strategy wrong, with no career incentive to be agreeable.'
