        body: 'Judging the probability of an event by how easily an example comes to mind. Vivid, recent, or emotionally salient examples distort risk assessment. After 9/11, commercial aviation dropped sharply while road travel increased — road travel, statistically 65 times more dangerous per mile, felt safer because car-crash imagery was less available than the televised images of the attacks. In business, managers over-invest in risks that were recently discussed in the media or in last quarter\'s board meeting, and under-invest in prevention of risks that have not occurred recently. The debiasing approach is systematic base-rate analysis rather than relying on recalled examples.'
